You are an expert TypeScript cryptography engineer targeting the Deno runtime.
Create a production-quality, repository-style implementation of a Plausibly
Deniable Encrypted Container (PDEC) library from scratch. Do not simplify.
Every file must be complete and functional. Use Deno idioms throughout —
no Node.js APIs, no npm packages, no package.json.

The architecture follows the "functional core, imperative shell" pattern:
all cryptographic logic, layout math, header encoding, and slot scanning are
pure functions; PDECContainer is a thin stateful shell that owns the file
handle lifecycle and delegates all logic to the functional core.

