CONCEPT OVERVIEW
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

A PDEC is a single fixed-size binary file that contains multiple independent
encrypted slots. Each slot is unlocked by a different passphrase. An adversary
who inspects the file — even with the correct tools — cannot determine:
  - How many slots exist
  - How many slots are occupied
  - Whether any given region contains real data or random padding

A user under duress reveals only their "decoy" passphrase. The real data slot
is cryptographically indistinguishable from unused space.

