ARCHITECTURE: FUNCTIONAL CORE, IMPERATIVE SHELL
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

The library is divided into two strict layers. No function in the functional
core may access Deno.open, Deno.fsync, or any IRandomAccessHandle. All IO
is performed exclusively by PDECContainer and the IO backends.

FUNCTIONAL CORE — pure functions, no IO, no side effects:
  src/core/layout.ts        computeLayout, slotOffset, validateLayout
  src/core/header.ts        buildHeader, parseHeader
  src/core/constants.ts     MAGIC, VERSION, HEADER_SIZE, buildAAD
  src/crypto/kdf.ts         deriveKeyArgon2, deriveKeyScrypt, withKey
  src/crypto/random.ts      randomBytes, shuffleIndices, jitter
  src/crypto/schemes/*.ts   ICryptoScheme plain objects (no class syntax)
  src/crypto/registry.ts    resolve(id), register(scheme)
  src/slot/scanner.ts       scanSlots, tryDecryptSlot
  src/slot/allocator.ts     findFreeSlot, buildSlotAAD
  src/passphrase/*.ts       validatePassphrase, normalizePassphrase, estimateEntropy

IMPERATIVE SHELL — owns state, performs IO:
  src/core/container.ts     PDECContainer class
  src/io/file-handle.ts     FileHandle
  src/io/buffer-handle.ts   BufferHandle

PDECContainer's methods do exactly three things:
  1. Read raw bytes from the handle at computed offsets
  2. Pass those bytes to functional core functions
  3. Write the returned bytes back to the handle

No encryption, decryption, layout math, or header parsing logic lives
inside container.ts. It is glue only.

