CONTAINER FILE FORMAT
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

The container is a flat binary file of exactly `totalSize` bytes.
No global header. No plaintext magic bytes. No slot count field.
The entire file must be indistinguishable from random bytes without a key.

Each slot layout:

  [ ENCRYPTED BLOB | RANDOM PADDING ]
   ↑                ↑
   HEADER_SIZE +    slotSize − (HEADER_SIZE + payloadLen + tagBytes)
   payloadLen +
   tagBytes bytes

The encrypted blob is one AEAD unit: encrypt(header_bytes || payload_bytes).
The 16-byte tag is written immediately after the ciphertext.
The remainder of the slot is fresh CSPRNG random bytes on every write.

Slot header layout (plaintext, inside the AEAD):

  Offset  Size  Field
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   0       4    Magic: 0xDE 0xC0 0x1A 0x57  (verified post-decrypt)
   4       1    Format version: 0x01
   5       1    Scheme ID
   6       2    Reserved: 0x00 0x00
   8      16    KDF salt (random per write)
   24     12    Nonce/IV (12 bytes; XChaCha20 24-byte nonce stored in
                the payload section, not the header)
   36      4    Payload byte length (uint32 LE, DataView)
   40      8    Write timestamp Unix ms (uint64 LE, two uint32 DataView writes)
   48     16    Random slot nonce (anti-correlation between slots)
  ─────────
   64     HEADER_SIZE

AEAD additional data (6 bytes, not encrypted):
  buildAAD(slotIndex, schemeId) = MAGIC(4) || slotIndex(1) || schemeId(1)

KDF input: encode(normalizePassphrase(passphrase)) || slotNonce bytes.

On AEAD tag failure, tryDecryptSlot returns undefined (never throws).
The magic check (0xDE C0 1A 57) is performed after successful AEAD
decryption as a secondary sanity check.

