  src/io/types.ts:

  export interface IRandomAccessHandle {
    read(offset: number, length: number): Promise<Uint8Array>;
    write(offset: number, data: Uint8Array): Promise<void>;
    sync(): Promise<void>;
    close(): Promise<void>;
    readonly size: number;
  }

  src/io/file-handle.ts — FileHandle:
    - Constructor takes an already-opened Deno.FsFile and its size
    - read():  seek then loop Deno.FsFile.read() until buffer full
    - write(): seek then loop Deno.FsFile.write() until all bytes written
    - sync():  Deno.fsync(this.file.rid)
    - close(): this.file.close()
    - Wrap Deno errors in IOError

    Full read loop (Deno.FsFile.read returns number | null at the boundary —
    convert to undefined immediately, do not propagate null inward):

      await this.file.seek(offset, Deno.SeekMode.Start);
      let pos = 0;
      while (pos < length) {
        const n = await this.file.read(buf.subarray(pos));
        // Deno runtime returns null at EOF — convert to undefined at boundary
        if (n === null || n === undefined) throw new IOError('Unexpected EOF');
        pos += n;
      }

  src/io/buffer-handle.ts — BufferHandle:
    - Constructor takes a Uint8Array of fixed size
    - All operations synchronous internally, wrapped in Promise.resolve()
    - sync(): no-op
    - Used exclusively in tests

