- Output every file in full. Never truncate. No placeholder comments such as
  '// ... rest of implementation'. Every function body must be complete.
- Only the two npm dependencies in deno.json may be used. No others.
- All imports must use specifiers from deno.json's imports map for external
  deps, and relative paths with explicit .ts extensions for internal ones:
    import { buildAAD } from '../core/constants.ts';
- Use Uint8Array everywhere in the public API. Never expose Buffer or string
  for binary data parameters or return values.
- All async functions must be properly awaited. No floating promises.
- Use DataView for all multi-byte integer encoding (little-endian).
- For uint64 timestamps: write as two uint32 values (low and high word)
  since JS lacks native uint64 primitives.
- Use satisfies ICryptoScheme on every scheme object declaration.
- Every exported symbol must have a JSDoc comment.
- Prefer undefined over null everywhere in library code. Never use null as
  a return value, parameter type, or variable initializer. The sole exception
  is at external API boundaries where the Deno runtime or an npm module
  returns null — convert to undefined immediately at that boundary and never
  propagate null further into the codebase.
- deno lint must pass with zero warnings on the completed output.
- deno fmt must produce no diffs on the completed output.
